\title{infereportR: Tables, Text and Figures for Statistical Results}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.svg}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Formats finalized statistical results as tables, text and figures. Results follow the common result contract of 'infercalcR'; stored estimates, intervals, p-values and method metadata are reported at full precision and are never recomputed. Its figure layer extends 'ggplot2' with a black-and-white theme for papers, following the figure rules of the Publication Manual, 7th edition, of the American Psychological Association (2020, ISBN:978-1-4338-3216-1), and for slides; with scales that replace color with line types, point shapes and hatch patterns; and with direct labels and size presets. Inference layers run explicitly named 'infercalcR' procedures, label them with the package's own display strings and keep the full results retrievable from the figure; annotation layers draw precomputed results at explicit positions. A character mode redraws plots on a monospaced text grid in the style of 1980s home computers.
